# AirSkyBoat

FFXI server emulator (LandSandBoat fork). Era accuracy: `modules/era/`. Live-server QoL: `modules/custom/`.

If you are an AI agent, read `documentation/ai_agents/README.md` first. Style: [LSB Development Guide](https://github.com/LandSandBoat/server/wiki/Development-Guide). Workflow: [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/LandSandBoat/server/blob/base/CONTRIBUTING.md).

## Do

- Copy nearby scripts for syntax, enums, and formatting. Ask when retail behavior is unclear.
- Prefer Interaction Framework for new quest/mission NPC logic.
- Cite sources in code comments or commit messages (wiki, captures, SE posts, patch dates). PR text is not enough.
- Put live-server QoL in `modules/custom/` and enable it in local `modules/init.txt`.
- Prefer small, focused changes. Ask before large rewrites or IF migrations.

## Do not

- Invent FFXI mechanics, timings, event IDs, drops, or job math.
- Use DarkStar (`dsp.*`), Windower, or unrelated Lua addon patterns. Match this tree.
- Put non-retail QoL in `scripts/` or `modules/era/`.
- Convert old NPC scripts to IF without captures and wiki triangulation.
- Edit `settings/*.lua` except `settings/default/` (local settings are gitignored).
- Touch `ext/` or `dev.docker-compose.yml` unless asked (copy Compose changes to `docker-compose.yml`).
- Commit secrets, `tools/config.yaml`, `sql/backups/`, `modules/init.txt`, or live DB dumps.
- Publish exploit details in issues/PRs/chat; flag them privately.
- Deploy, pull, or restart the live map process unless asked. Use the personal `ssh-live` skill.

## Verify

Mark unverified or 1-to-1 conversion work in comments. Remind the user to check the game client, retail captures, `../FFXI-EventsDump`, BG-Wiki, and FFXIclopedia.
